[b]Skyrim Together Reborn Launcher[/b]

Play Skyrim Together Reborn with your friends — on Windows or Linux — in one click. No Vortex, no Mod Organizer 2, no manual file shuffling: STR Launcher finds your Skyrim, downloads and installs the mod for you, checks that everything is ready, and gets you straight into a multiplayer session.

One self-contained program — no installer, no runtime dependencies — and every change it makes can be undone with one click.

[b]Requirements[/b]

[list]
[*]Skyrim Special Edition ([b]Steam, v1.6 or newer[/b]), launched once through Steam first — reach the main menu, then quit. The Anniversary Upgrade DLC is not needed and is best disabled.
[*]A free [url=https://www.nexusmods.com]Nexus Mods[/url] account (for the automatic downloads).
[*]Windows 8.1 or newer, or Linux (Steam Deck works great).
[/list]

[b]Installation[/b]

[list]
[*]Download [b]STR Launcher[/b] from the Files tab and run it. It finds your Skyrim install automatically.
[*]Open Settings → Nexus Mods and paste your Nexus API key (Nexus account settings → Personal API keys → Generate personal key). One-time only; the key is stored on your PC.
[*]Press [b]Install Skyrim Together Reborn[/b] and wait for the readiness checklist to go green — it checks your game version, Address Library, plugins and (on Linux) Proton, so nothing fails silently.
[*]Press [b]Launch Together[/b]. In-game, press [b]F2[/b] to open the multiplayer menu, create a party, and invite your friends.
[/list]

Finish the Helgen intro [b]before[/b] connecting to a server — see the official [url=https://wiki.tiltedphoques.com/tilted-online/general-information/playguide]play guide[/url] (one minute, well worth it).

[b]No Nexus API key? Offline mode[/b]

Download the two archives manually, drop them in under Settings → Offline mode, and press Install:

[list]
[*][url=https://www.nexusmods.com/skyrimspecialedition/mods/69993?tab=files]Skyrim Together Reborn[/url]
[*][url=https://www.nexusmods.com/skyrimspecialedition/mods/32444?tab=files]Address Library[/url]
[/list]

[b]Main features[/b]

[list]
[*][b]One-click install[/b] — auto-detects your Skyrim and installs Skyrim Together Reborn + Address Library through the Nexus API.
[*][b]Readiness checklist[/b] — verifies game version, Address Library, plugins and Proton before every launch, so nothing fails silently.
[*][b]Launch Together[/b] — starts the modded game straight from the launcher.
[*][b]Full undo[/b] — removed Creation Club content goes to a backup folder, a manifest records every file the launcher touched, and [b]Undo[/b] restores your Skyrim to exactly how it was.
[*][b]Offline mode[/b] — no Nexus API key needed; point it at the two archives you downloaded yourself.
[*][b]Steam Deck friendly[/b] — works on Linux and the Deck out of the box, no custom launch options required.
[/list]

[b]Linux / Steam Deck[/b]

The launcher pins [b]GE-Proton 10[/b] automatically (GE-Proton 11 crashes Skyrim Together 1.8) and offers two launch modes — replace the Skyrim launcher, or add a separate [b]"Skyrim Together Reborn"[/b] entry to your Steam library with its own artwork. Both are fully reversible with Undo.

GOG/Epic copies: automatic Steam detection and launch integrations are Steam-only, but the installer still works — point it at your SkyrimSE.exe under Settings → Game → Browse.

[b]Good to know[/b]

[list]
[*][b]Same version, no extra mods.[/b] All players must run the same Skyrim Together version (use Check updates), and extra mods are the #1 cause of crashes with Skyrim Together.
[*][b]Steam Deck black screen?[/b] Remove any old custom launch options for Skyrim in Steam — this launcher doesn't need them.
[*][b]"Skyrim Together is not running!"[/b] Press [b]Undo[/b], then [b]Install[/b] again.
[/list]

